    "name": "Yunoyado Onsen-Jiaoxi",
    "detail": "Fortunately, I was able to stay in a classic double room for about 3,100 yen per night. The bed was large, and there was enough space in the bathtub for a person 180 cm tall to stretch their legs comfortably. It was clean, and considering the cost performance, I was very satisfied. Additionally, for me as a Japanese person, having a washlet was a plus point. One thing to note is that the amenities are limited to shampoo, body soap, and hand soap. Also, breakfast is served in a set meal style, where you can choose one main dish from three options: fish and two types of meat dishes. While there is an all-you-can-eat coffee machine, juice station, ice cream, and cereal, there is no all-you-can-eat option for the main food items, which might be a disadvantage for those who prefer a buffet-style breakfast. However, the set meals are generous in portion, so unless you're a big eater, I think you will be satisfied. Personally, I was very satisfied with the hotel.",
